
What changes vs what stays the same
Stays exactly the same ✅
Everything from S3 onwards is untouched:

S3 → SNS → SQS → image_recognition Lambda
→ Rekognition → DynamoDB → Athena → QuickSight
What changes — the ingestion layer
Currently:

curl (human) → API Gateway → ImageGetAndSaveLambda → S3
With IoT cameras:

Street camera → AWS IoT Core → S3  (direct, no API Gateway needed)
The IoT Architecture
Street Camera (Raspberry Pi / IP camera)
    │
    │  MQTT over TLS (port 8883)
    ▼
AWS IoT Core
    │  IoT Rule: "SELECT * FROM 'cameras/+/image'"
    │
    ├──► S3 Action → sagemaker-eu-central-1-015337708931/<camera-id>/<timestamp>.jpg
    │                  ↓
    │              S3 PUT event → SNS → SQS → image_recognition Lambda (unchanged)
    │
    └──► DynamoDB Action → log raw device metadata (optional)
Specific changes needed
1. New: IoT Stack (new CDK stack)
# iot/infrastructure.py
- aws_iot.CfnThing          # register each camera as an IoT Thing
- aws_iot.CfnPolicy         # allow camera to publish to MQTT topic
- aws_iot.CfnTopicRule      # rule: on image message → write to S3
- aws_iot.CfnCertificate    # X.509 cert per camera (device auth)
2. Remove: ImageGetAndSaveLambda + API Gateway (APIStack)
No longer needed — cameras push directly to IoT Core which writes to S3.

3. Change: S3 key naming convention
Currently: name parameter from curl (e.g. car1.jpg) With IoT: <camera-id>/<timestamp>.jpg (e.g. cam-a3-ffm-001/2026-05-24T06:00:00Z.jpg)

Update image_recognition.py to parse the richer key:

# Extract camera ID from S3 key
# key = "cam-a3-ffm-001/2026-05-24T06:00:00Z.jpg"
camera_id = key.split("/")[0]
timestamp = key.split("/")[1].replace(".jpg", "")
4. Change: DynamoDB item — add camera metadata
db_item = {
    "image":     {"S": key},
    "labels":    {"S": str(db_result)},
    "camera_id": {"S": camera_id},      # NEW
    "timestamp": {"S": timestamp},       # NEW
    "location":  {"S": camera_location}, # NEW — from IoT Thing attributes
}
5. Camera device code (runs on the camera)
# Runs on Raspberry Pi / embedded Linux
